164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The proposed model focuses on reward-based crowdfunding, where contributors receive non-monetary incentives, such as merchandise, premiere invitations, or even small on-screen roles. This approach simultaneously serves as a funding mechanism, audience-building tool, and marketing strategy. It encourages early validation of scripts and concepts by allowing potential audiences to decide which projects deserve to be made. Moreover, crowdfunding fosters a sense of ownership among backers, turning them into both consumers and promoters \(prosumers\) of the film.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In addition to financial support, this model unlocks intangible benefits greater audience engagement, cultural diversity, and inclusivity in storytelling. As OTT platforms expand globally, crowdfunding provides a viable, community-driven alternative to traditional top-down finance models, empowering independent creators while strengthening audience creator connections.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
